From: 3mro777o <3mro777o@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 09:06:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nir/opt_varyings: use nir_src_rewrite when shrinking varying
 arrays

When remove_dead_varyings shrinks an array to a single element, it
resets the indirect offset to zero by assigning
*offset_src = nir_src_for_ssa(...). That overwrites the src without
removing it from the use list of the old SSA value, which corrupts
the list.

nir_validate catches the corruption, and RADV crashes when it links
tessellation shaders.

Use nir_src_rewrite() instead, since it keeps the use lists up to
date. The same bug was present in two places: the load case and the
store case.

Generated-by: LLM
Fixes: 1559e1477076 ("nir/opt_varyings: shrink pathological varying arrays to 1 element")
(cherry picked from commit 84b0eb6ba8310e8a93b92fe11e76e0f4c2cfe7dc)

Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45704>
(cherry picked from commit cdbaf5f9ec91a89dfb2f39033384621f6c68e34e)
---
 src/compiler/nir/nir_opt_varyings.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/compiler/nir/nir_opt_varyings.c b/src/compiler/nir/nir_opt_varyings.c
index 014522760ff..823be844b72 100644
--- a/src/compiler/nir/nir_opt_varyings.c
+++ b/src/compiler/nir/nir_opt_varyings.c
@@ -2389,7 +2389,7 @@ remove_dead_varyings(struct linkage_info *linkage,
                            assert(elem == 0);
 
                            b->cursor = nir_before_instr(&load->instr);
-                           *offset_src = nir_src_for_ssa(nir_imm_int(b, 0));
+                           nir_src_rewrite(offset_src, nir_imm_int(b, 0));
 
                            /* Reduce the number of slots to 1. */
                            nir_io_semantics sem =
@@ -2490,7 +2490,7 @@ remove_dead_varyings(struct linkage_info *linkage,
                         nir_if *if_eq =
                            nir_push_if(b, nir_ieq_imm(b, offset.def,
                                                       direct_index));
-                        *offset_src = nir_src_for_ssa(nir_imm_int(b, 0));
+                        nir_src_rewrite(offset_src, nir_imm_int(b, 0));
                         nir_instr_move(b->cursor, &store->instr);
                         b->cursor = nir_after_instr(&store->instr);
                         nir_pop_if(b, if_eq);
